      "writtenOn": "2026-07-19T10:00:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Two-tier approach:\n------------------\nNow (this patch): \ngsh_mem_stats_update_free() already has an underflow-clamp when current_active_bytes \u003c size (freeing more than was ever accounted). Today that\u0027s silently clamped to 0. Added a LogWarn there — it\u0027s a free, always-on tripwire that fires on the most common mismatch pattern (freeing against a component that never had this memory).\n\nFollow-up (separate patch):\nFor a precise, exhaustive check, add a debug/test-only shadow table (pointer -\u003e mem_comp, gated behind a build/runtime flag like _INTERNAL_STATD) populated in gsh_mem_stats_update_alloc() and checked and erased in gsh_mem_stats_update_free(). Mismatch -\u003e LogCrit. Run the full test suite once with it enabled to catch every mismatch precisely.",
      "parentUuid": "830f53d3_c901eece",
      "revId": "0f832a03c2a3e6ae55223f25ac0764712c85dff7",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
